BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 750 Td
(Account Closure Policy) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Apex Global Bank - Retail and Institutional Banking) Tj T*
(Document ID: POL-ACC-004 | Version 3.1 | Owner: Operations Control) Tj T*
(Illustrative policy for the Finova demo workspace. Not legal or regulatory advice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Purpose) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This policy defines how customer accounts are closed, whether the closure is requested by the) Tj T*
(customer or initiated by the bank, so that balances are settled correctly, records are) Tj T*
(retained, and no closure is used to hide suspicious activity.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Customer-Requested Closure) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. The customer submits a closure request through net banking, the mobile app, or a signed) Tj T*
(branch form.) Tj T*
(2. Support verifies identity using two factors: registered mobile OTP plus one of date of) Tj T*
(birth, PAN, or the last transaction amount.) Tj T*
(3. The account must have no pending debits, no open disputes, no active standing instructions,) Tj T*
(and no linked loan or overdraft balance.) Tj T*
(4. Any remaining credit balance is transferred to a verified account in the customer's own) Tj T*
(name. Cash payout is allowed only up to INR 50,000 at a branch.) Tj T*
(5. Cheque books and debit cards are cancelled in the core system on the same day.) Tj T*
(6. The customer receives a closure confirmation letter within 2 business days.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Standard turnaround: closure is completed within 5 business days of a complete request.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Bank-Initiated Closure) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The bank may close an account when:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- KYC remains incomplete 90 days after the re-KYC due date, after three written reminders.) Tj T*
(- The account is dormant for more than 24 months with a zero balance.) Tj T*
(- The account is linked to confirmed fraud or a regulatory directive.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A bank-initiated closure requires approval from a Branch Manager and the Compliance Officer.) Tj T*
(The customer receives at least 30 days' written notice, except where a regulatory or) Tj T*
(law-enforcement directive requires immediate action.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Restrictions) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- An account under an open fraud case, AML review, or legal hold must not be closed. The) Tj T*
(closure request is parked until Compliance releases it.) Tj T*
(- Accounts with a risk score of 80 or above must be reviewed by the Fraud Operations team) Tj T*
(before closure.) Tj T*
(- Joint accounts require consent from all holders.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Record Retention) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Account opening documents, KYC records and transaction history are retained for 10 years after) Tj T*
(the closure date. Closed accounts are flagged read-only and cannot be reactivated; a returning) Tj T*
(customer must open a new account with fresh KYC.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Roles and Responsibilities) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- Support Executive: verifies identity, checks closure prerequisites, raises the request.) Tj T*
(- Operations: settles balances, cancels instruments, closes the account in core banking.) Tj T*
(- Compliance: approves bank-initiated closures and releases accounts on hold.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
